      "title": "Australian government concedes no scientific consensus on social media harms for teenagers – but ‘credible risks’ justify ban",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/30/social-media-ban-australia-high-court-mental-health-risks-teens",
      "description": "<p>Commonwealth tells high court its proposed laws to let users opt out of algorithms would ultimately have the same effect as the ban</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>The Australian government has conceded it implemented the “world-leading” under-16s social media ban before there was scientific consensus on the link between mental health harms and social media use, but argued the “credible risks” of issues such as addictive behaviours and anxiety justify the policy.</p><p>In its defence against a high court challenge of the ban, the government has also argued its proposed <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/08/australia-social-media-algorithm-switch-off-opt-out-digital-duty-of-care\">digital duty of care legislation</a>, allowing users to opt out of social media features such as algorithms, would ultimately have the same effect as the ban, if implemented.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/30/social-media-ban-australia-high-court-mental-health-risks-teens\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-29T15:00:56"
    },
    {
      "title": "Guardian Essential poll: Coalition’s primary vote sinks to lowest ever as majority support hardline immigration ideas",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/29/guardian-essential-poll-coalitions-primary-vote-sinks-to-lowest-ever-as-majority-support-hardline-immigration-ideas",
      "description": "<p>More than half of Australians want to see the country’s migrant intake lowered while One Nation’s primary vote climbs to 25%</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>The Coalition has failed to capitalise on growing criticism of Labor, with the opposition stuck at its lowest-ever primary vote in the Guardian Essential poll.</p><p>The poll also shows more than half of all Australians want immigration cut and have voiced support for hardline enforcement, such as forced deportation.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/29/guardian-essential-poll-coalitions-primary-vote-sinks-to-lowest-ever-as-majority-support-hardline-immigration-ideas\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-29T15:00:55"
    },
