      "title": "Imams’ council condemns Melbourne Islamic preacher’s call to ‘take up arms’ against enemies",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/29/imam-council-melbourne-islamic-preacher-abu-ahmad-video-take-up-arms-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Independent MP Allegra Spender says the comments reinforce the need for stronger protection against hate speech</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Australia’s peak body for imams says it is “deeply concerned” about reports a Melbourne-based Islamic preacher called for followers to “take up arms against his enemies” and not take “Jews and the Christians for friends”.</p><p>The Australian National Imams’ Council (ANIC) released a statement on Tuesday after Nine newspapers revealed the preacher who goes by the name Abu Ahmad made the comments during a sermon in July.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/29/imam-council-melbourne-islamic-preacher-abu-ahmad-video-take-up-arms-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
